        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Summary\r\n17 Bishop Street is a beautifully restored four-bedroom townhouse offering character, flexibility and a surprisingly spacious interior, all within walking distance of every amenity Cobh has to offer. Thoughtfully renovated to a high standard, the property combines period charm with stylish modern finishes, creating a home that is both warm and practical.\r\nUpon entering, you are welcomed into a bright entrance hall leading to a versatile ground floor layout. This level comprises a utility room, guest WC and laundry area, together with a flexible room that could be used as a home office, playroom, additional reception room or fifth bedroom, depending on your needs. To the rear is a beautifully presented open-plan kitchen, dining and living area complete with a solid fuel stove, creating the perfect space for everyday living and entertaining.\r\nThe first floor features a spacious sitting room, a contemporary family bathroom and two generously sized bedrooms, one of which is currently used as a home office. On the second floor are two further double bedrooms, including one with an adjoining dressing room or study, together with a large family bathroom finished to an exceptional standard.\r\nOne of the standout features of this home is the impressive rear garden. Arranged over three levels, it has been thoughtfully landscaped to enjoy the sun throughout the day, with multiple seating areas creating ideal spaces for outdoor dining, relaxing and entertaining. At the top of the garden is a purpose-built workshop complete with electricity, making it ideal as a home office, hobby room, studio or additional workspace.\r\nRarely does a townhouse in the heart of Cobh offer such generous outdoor space combined with beautifully presented accommodation. Finished to an exceptional standard throughout, this is a turnkey home that perfectly balances character, comfort and convenience.\r\n\r\nProperty Features\r\n•\tBeautifully restored townhouse finished to a high standard\r\n•\tFour bedrooms\r\n•\tThree bathrooms, including guest WC\r\n•\tFlexible ground floor room suitable as a home office, playroom, fifth bedroom or home business\r\n•\tOpen-plan kitchen, dining and living area with solid fuel stove\r\n•\tSpacious first-floor sitting room\r\n•\tLandscaped rear garden arranged over three levels\r\n•\tMultiple sun-filled seating and entertaining areas\r\n•\tPurpose-built workshop with electricity\r\n•\tIdeal workshop, home office, studio or hobby room\r\n•\tGas fired central heating\r\n•\tPVC double glazed windows\r\n•\tBER C2 – BER No. 108907\r\n•\tWalking distance to Cobh town centre, schools, shops and transport links\r\n•\tTastefully decorated throughout\r\n•\tTurnkey condition"
      },
